Symbol library — attribution and licensing
==========================================

The symbols in this directory are an INDEPENDENT, CLEAN-ROOM drawing of the
graphical symbols for diagrams defined by EN 60617 (= IEC 60617; Czech
ČSN EN 60617). They are the original work of this project, © 2026 miromraz,
and are released under the MIT License (see lib/LICENSE) — the same license as
the code.

Clean-room process
------------------
The drawings were produced without copying any other vendor's symbol drawings:

  1. A facts-only specification was written for each symbol, recording ONLY
     non-expressive facts drawn from the EN 60617 standard: the symbol's name,
     the standard clause number, the ordered connection points (pin positions
     and pin NUMBER order, so wiring matches the standard), the overall drawn
     size, and any letters/markings the standard places inside the symbol
     (e.g. "V", "M", "3~"). No drawing data — no primitives, polylines, arcs,
     line widths, fills, fonts or text positions — was recorded or carried.
  2. Separate drawing teams rendered those facts into ProfiCAD-format .ppd
     files. The drawing teams had NO access to any third-party symbol library
     and worked only from the facts specification.

Because the pin positions and pin-number order come from the EN 60617 facts,
drawings made with this library carry the standard's connection numbering; the
geometry (shapes, line widths, proportions, label placement) is this project's
own and differs from any particular vendor's rendering.

